-- title:
--   Finite étaleness of the Kummer algebra R[X]/(Xⁿ-u)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $n$ be a natural number and let $u \in R$. Assume that the image of $n$ under the canonical map $\mathbb{N} \to R$ is a unit of $R$, and that $u$ is a unit of $R$. Then the $R$-algebra $\mathrm{AdjoinRoot}(X^n - C\,u)$, that is the quotient $R[X]/(X^n - u)$ of the polynomial ring by the ideal generated by the monic polynomial $X^n - C\,u$, satisfies both `Algebra.Etale R` (it is a formally étale and finitely presented $R$-algebra) and `Module.Finite R` (it is finitely generated as an $R$-module); the conclusion is the conjunction of these two assertions. No nonvanishing hypothesis on $n$ is imposed: if $n = 0$ then the hypothesis that $n \cdot 1_R$ is a unit forces $R$, and hence the quotient, to be the zero ring, for which both assertions hold trivially.
--
--   This is the assertion that a Kummer algebra, the coordinate ring of the $\mu_n$-torsor of $n$-th roots of a unit, is finite étale over the base as soon as $n$ is invertible. It is used in the construction of étale, faithfully flat, finite extensions over which a given unit acquires an $n$-th root, and in the identification of the integral closure in such an extension with the subalgebra generated by a root.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AdjoinRoot_etale_and_finite_X_pow_sub_C_of_isUnit.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
